        "id": "p27-challenge-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "If a die is rolled, what is the probability that a six is not obtained?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{5}{6}$",
          "worked": "The favourable outcomes are $1,2,3,4,5$: five of the six equally likely outcomes.\n\n$$P(\\text{not six})=\\frac{5}{6}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-challenge-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If two dice are rolled, what is the probability that no sixes are obtained?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{25}{36}$",
          "worked": "The two-dice array has $6\\times6=36$ equally likely outcomes. Excluding the row and column containing a six leaves $5\\times5=25$ favourable outcomes.\n\n$$P(\\text{no sixes})=\\frac{25}{36}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
